# The build context is the PARENT directory (see docker-compose.yml), so without this file
# every sibling checkout -- worktrees, .venvs, node_modules, data-lake's Parquet archive --
# is sent to the builder, and `COPY data-lake` bakes ~2 GB of it into the image. BuildKit
# reads `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` from beside the Dockerfile in place of a context-root
# `.dockerignore`, which a parent directory shared by every project cannot carry.
#
# Allowlist: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs. A new
# COPY source has to be added here too, or the build fails with "not found".
*
!data-lake/pyproject.toml
!data-lake/README.md
!data-lake/src
!ibkr_trader/pyproject.toml
!ibkr_trader/uv.lock
!ibkr_trader/README.md
!ibkr_trader/src
!ibkr_trader/alembic.ini
!ibkr_trader/migrations
**/__pycache__
